  "description": "The RUUT is an exceptionally versatile gravel bike thanks to the unique TwinTip fork – a feature that allows you to fine tune the handling and set up your bike exactly the way you like – relaxed or racy, the choice is yours to make at any point in time.\n\nThe RUUT has always been one step ahead of its time, and the third generation of the aluminum version is no exception. It features a seamless integration of the bottom bracket and seat tube, and a hidden toolbox on the underside of the frame that comes with a multitool and a chain tool – the two things you need most on a long day out, always on board. The design offers generous tire clearance and room for large chainrings. Cables run through the headset bearings and the ICR stem, the frame is ready for an internally routed dropper post, and the UDH hanger and thru axles front and rear finish the job. Add the full carbon TwinTip fork and you get a look that's as crisp as your confidence.\n\nThe RUUT AL1 2X is the one for riders who mix tarmac, group rides and gravel in a single week. Shifting is handled by a tried-and-tested Shimano GRX 2x11 groupset, with a 46/30 crankset that keeps the steps between gears small on the road and still gets you up the steepest gravel climbs. Clutch-equipped GRX derailleurs keep the chain calm when the surface gets rough, and GRX levers are shaped for braking from the hoods on long descents. The bike rolls on Reynolds G30 wheels backed by a lifetime guarantee and fast rolling 45 mm WTB Vulpine tires, tubeless ready out of the box. All black, nothing to distract from the lines. Ideal for those who prefer the flexibility of a double chainring for tackling varied terrain.",
